    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "We at Felicity Fox are delighted to present to the market this mid terrace 2 bedroom period home.  This property has been completely refurbished with architect supervision and has a single storey extension to the rear and an attic conversion.  With many contemporary features throughout this house and a sunny garden to the rear with a paved dining area with pergola the property is sure to appeal to the discerning buyer. \r\nOn walking through the front door the hallway leads to a sitting room featuring ceiling coving, built-in shelving and a fireplace with a wood burning stove.  At the end of the hallway is a lobby with a guest WC on one side and a large storage cupboard on the other.  The kitchen/living room is in a large, high ceiling extension to the rear of the house.  The kitchen is fitted with a range of wall and floor units and integrated appliances.  A utility room is located off the kitchen and is plumbed for a washing machine and tumble dryer.  The living area is full of natural light with Velux windows and floor to ceiling sliding door allowing the daylight to flood in.  There is underfloor heating in this room.  Upstairs, is a fully modernised bathroom with a bath.  The master bedroom to the front of the house has built-in wardrobes and an en suite shower room.  The second bedroom is to the rear of the house and has built-in wardrobes.  A fixed stairs leads to the attic room which is dormer style and has plenty of under eaves storage.  Outside, the fully landscaped rear garden has a lawn laid with astroturf, raised flower beds with mature planting and a paved dining area with a pergola.  To the front, a small garden is bounded by iron railings and a footpath leads to the front door.  Parking is on street with resident permit.\r\nMerton Avenue is a mature residential street off the South Circular Road.  The area is host to a range of cafés, bars and restaurants such as Noshington and Marlowe.  The location is particularly convenient with ease of access to excellent transport links such as the LUAS and various bus routes.  St Stephen's Green and Grafton Street are within walking distance.  St James’s Hospital, The Coombe Hospital and the New Children’s Hospital are also close by."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall     5.10m x 2.51m\r\nTimber flooring. Ceiling coving. Understairs storage.\r\n\r\nSitting room     5.35m x 3.60m\r\nTimber flooring. Ceiling coving. Recessed lighting. Fireplace with wood burning stove and marble hearth. Built-in shelving.\r\n\r\nLobby     2.15m x 2.09m\r\nTimber flooring.  Access to storage press.\r\n\r\nGuest bathroom     1.60m x 1.30m\r\nTiled floor. WC. Wash hand basin.\r\n\r\n\r\nKitchen/livng room     5.90m x 4.64m\r\nTiled floor. Underfloor heating. Range of wall and floor units. Integrated electric oven, grill, microwave, hob, fridge freezer and dishwasher. Timber flooring. Recessed lighting. Velux windows. Sliding door to rear garden.\r\n\r\nUtility room     1.50m x 1.30m\r\nTiled floor. Built-in shelving. Plumbing for washing machine and tumble dryer. Cupboard housing water storage tank.\r\n\r\nUpstairs\r\n\r\nLanding     2.58m x 2.13m\r\nCarpet flooring. Stairs to attic room.\r\n\r\nMaster bedroom     3.80m x 2.19m plus 2.49m x 2.48m\r\nCarpet flooring. Built-in wardrobes.\r\n\r\nEn suite     2.48m x 0.67m\r\nTiled floor. Tiled walls. Shower enclosure with Monsoon shower head. WC. Wash hand basin.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2     3.08m x 2.49m \r\nCarpet flooring. Recessed lighting. Built-in wardrobes. Original fireplace. Gas boiler.\r\n\r\nBathroom     2.35m x 1.43m\r\nTiled floor. Part tiled walls. WC. Wash hand basin. Bath with Triton electric shower overhead. \r\n\r\nAttic room     4.17m x 2.55m\r\nCarpet flooring. Recessed lighting. Velux window. Under eaves storage.\r\n\r\nOutside\r\n\r\nRear garden     5.40m x 3.29m\r\nPorcelain paving tiles. Raised flower beds with mature planting. Outside tap. Paved dining area with pergola. Astroturf lawn. \r\n\r\nFront garden     5.45m x 1.77m\r\nRailed garden. Cobblelock. Bin store."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "2 Bedrooms plus attic room\r\nExtended to rear\r\nUtility room\r\nFully refurbished in 2010 with architect supervision\r\nAttic conversion in 2021 with engineer supervision\r\nDouble glazed windows throughout\r\nGas fired central heating\r\nUnderfloor heating in kitchen/living room\r\nSunny rear garden with dining area and pergola\r\nOn street resident permit parking\r\nFloor area approximately 102sqm/1097sqft (not including attic)"
